    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (81.06) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Facing Brady Singer, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a potent combination of a favorable park factor, a solid order position in the two-hole, and a compelling BvP history that adds an 8% boost to his already high base projection. Following closely are **Cal Raleigh** (76.46) and **Daulton Varsho** (72.31), both of whom capitalize on plus matchups against vulnerable arms (Eric Lauer and Zack Littell, respectively). **Daulton Varsho** is particularly intriguing; while his base score is moderate, he carries a significant 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill level and a 10% platoon advantage, making him an elite utility play despite the inherent risks associated with his sprint speed-heavy profile.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest decision centered on the final bench spot, where **Gavin Sheets** (45.14) fell just short of displacing **Kyle Karros** (46.79). While **Gavin Sheets** offered a stronger platoon edge against Gabriel Hughes, his lower base projection and the negative impact of his seventh-order position ultimately kept him relegated to the bench. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Taylor Ward**, whose score of 50.44 is heavily dampened by a 19% penalty for facing the elite Tarik Skubal. Although **Taylor Ward** retains value via a platoon boost, he remains a high-risk start. Across the board, users should note that all projected order positions are currently \"Lineup Pending\"; should managers shift **Gleyber Torres** or **Geraldo Perdomo** out of their premium leadoff or two-hole spots, those efficiency scores will see immediate downward adjustments.",
